  "rootCause": "Lack of a formal process to regularly review and update the environmental aspects register, combined with inadequate training and responsibility assignment for integrating lifecycle perspective and new process evaluations into the environmental management system.",
  "actions": "1. Revise the Environmental Management System procedure to mandate annual (or trigger-based) review and update of the environmental aspects register, including integration of new processes. 2. Train relevant personnel on lifecycle perspective requirements per ISO 14001:2015 and assign clear ownership for register maintenance. 3. Conduct a comprehensive review of all current processes, including the three new ones (powder coating, acid etching, solvent degreasing), to identify and document associated environmental aspects and impacts using lifecycle thinking. 4. Implement a system to automatically flag new processes for environmental assessment during change control. 5. Document and retain updated register with supporting analysis and approval records.",
  "evidence": "Updated environmental aspects register with dated revisions, signed off by responsible personnel; training records for staff on lifecycle perspective and register maintenance; documented risk and impact assessments for the three new processes; change control logs showing integration of environmental review into process introduction; audit trail of review activities."
}
